  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 298,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Acid-base: ACIDEMIA or ALKALEMIA, and which value moved FIRST?",
   "lines": [
    "arterial blood gas (ABG): normal pH 7.35–7.45 · pCO2 = the lungs · HCO3 = the kidneys",
    "anion gap (AG) = Na − (Cl + HCO3): normal 12, minus 3 for every 10 g/L albumin below 40",
    "AG ↑ with a NORMAL pH and HCO3 → metabolic acidosis + metabolic alkalosis together"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_ac",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 738,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "ACIDEMIA: pH < 7.35",
   "lines": [
    "pCO2 ↑ → RESPIRATORY · HCO3 ↓ → METABOLIC"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_al",
   "x": 823,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 488,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "ALKALEMIA: pH > 7.45",
   "lines": [
    "pCO2 ↓ → RESPIRATORY · HCO3 ↑ → METABOLIC"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "t_ma",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 256,
   "w": 488,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "HCO3 ↓: METABOLIC acidosis · is the ANION GAP up?",
   "lines": [
    "expect pCO2 to fall 1 for every 1 HCO3 falls · off target → a SECOND disorder (aspirin: + respiratory alkalosis, pH > 7.45)",
    "pH < 7.10 or HCO3 < 10–12 → give sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO3) · careful: it makes CO2 and adds Na"
   ]
  },
